# ACT ONE

= Mara inherits a lighthouse nobody wants.

FADE IN:

EXT. ROCKY COASTLINE - DAWN #1#

Waves hammer black rocks. A lighthouse stands at the edge of the world, its lamp long dead.

MARA VOSS (30s, rain jacket, stubborn) climbs the slick path with a duffel bag and a ring of rusted keys.

MARA
(out of breath)
Of course it's uphill.

She stops. Looks up at the tower.

MARA (CONT'D)
Grandpa, you could have left me *anything* else.

[[Consider adding a gull here for comic relief.]]

INT. LIGHTHOUSE - GROUND FLOOR - CONTINUOUS

Dust. Old charts pinned to the walls. A kettle on a cold stove.

A voice crackles from an ancient RADIO on the desk.

RADIO (V.O.)
Keeper... come in, keeper...

Mara freezes.

MARA
That's not possible.

> CUT TO:

INT. LIGHTHOUSE - LAMP ROOM - NIGHT

The great lens, cracked but magnificent. Mara wipes it with her sleeve.

!SHE HEARS FOOTSTEPS BELOW.

ELIAS (O.S.)
You shouldn't be up there.

MARA
Who's there?

ELIAS ^
Someone who used to work here.

ELIAS steps into the lamplight. Seventies. Weathered. Holding a lantern.

ELIAS
Your grandfather kept that light burning for forty years. The ships still remember.

MARA
Ships don't remember things.

ELIAS
(smiling)
These ones do.

===

# ACT TWO

## The Storm

EXT. LIGHTHOUSE GALLERY - NIGHT

Rain lashes sideways. Mara and Elias haul a cable toward the lamp.

MARA
How long until the storm hits?

ELIAS
It already has.

~Keep the light, keeper, keep the light,
~Bring the lost ones home tonight.

> THE END <

/*
INT. CUT SCENE - DAY

This scene was cut but kept in the boneyard.
*/
